&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Director of Accounting to join our Accounting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Accounting will be the accounting lead for Oscar&#39;s recently acquired businesses and related platform operations, guiding their integration into Oscar&#39;s accounting and financial operations environment. You will oversee close processes, accounting and FinOps integrations, subledger activity, AR/AP commission accounting, and variance analytics in partnership with the business and FP&amp;amp;A. You will also help lead accounting integration for future M&amp;amp;A activity, including systems, data, controls, and reporting design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will report to the Deputy Controller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our New York City office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $180,504 - $236,912 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct end-to-end accounting for recently acquired businesses and related platform operations, including monthly and quarterly close, reconciliations, journal entries, supporting schedules, accounting conclusions, and control documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage accounting and financial operations integrations for acquired businesses, including process design, systems and data mapping, subledger flows, cross-functional handoffs, and transition readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead accounting operations for insurance-adjacent acquired businesses, including AR/AP accounting, insurance AMS accounting structure, data design, subledger journals, and reporting outputs needed by the business and FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide accounting leadership for SaaS and technology-enabled insurance platforms, including revenue, receivables, partner activity, and related platform accounting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review flux and variance analytics for acquired businesses, platform operations, and related integration activity; communicate key drivers and risks to Finance leadership and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accounting for future M&amp;amp;A activity, including diligence input, close-readiness, policy and control alignment, systems and data integration, and post-close accounting operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable policies, close calendars, reconciliations, controls, and process documentation; partner with Finance Operations, FP&amp;amp;A, Product/Engineering, Legal, Tax, and external auditors as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant accounting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience leading accounting close processes, reconciliations, journal entries, or financial reporting for a business line, subsidiary, platform, or acquired business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with accounting systems, subledgers, AR/AP accounting, revenue or receivables accounting, financial operations integrations, or data/process design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience preparing or reviewing flux and variance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a similar accounting leadership role at a health insurance, Insurtech, SaaS, or platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with M&amp;amp;A accounting, purchase accounting support, acquired-company integration, or post-close finance operations integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or managing insurance AMS, ERP, billing, receivables, payables, or subledger accounting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience with US-based insurance companies or insurance-adjacent businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading people and working collaboratively across accounting, finance, technology, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
