&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Director, Actuarial to join our Actuarial team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Actuarial, plays an important role in Oscar&#39;s actuarial department, leading a skilled team to manage Regional pricing across multiple states, drive strategic decisions and ensure regulatory compliance. Additionally, responsibilities will extend to mentoring and developing Oscar&#39;s team of actuaries. This team includes Associate Directors, Managers, and Analysts. Responsibilities will also involve collaborating closely with cross-functional teams in Finance, P&amp;amp;L, Product Development, and others. This actuarial leadership position makes critical actuarial decisions, has ownership of financial estimates and forecasts, and communicates recommendations to senior executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the VP, Actuarial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This position is fully remote and open to candidates residing in the U.S., &lt;strong&gt;excluding&lt;/strong&gt; Alaska; Delaware; Hawaii; Louisiana; Montana; North Dakota; Oklahoma; West Virginia; Wyoming; and U.S. Territories. Daily work is completed from your home office, with occasional travel required for team meetings and company events. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role in the states of California, Connecticut, New Jersey, New York, and Washington is: $198,720 - $260,820 per year. The base pay for this role in all other locations is: $178,848 - $234,738 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own decision-making responsibilities related to Actuarial methodologies, model enhancements, and business initiatives including but not limited to continually refining Actuarial approaches across the Director&#39;s portfolio and the business as a whole.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the end-to-end actuarial pricing processes within a specific portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote long-term goals and objectives that guide the strategic direction of the Actuarial function as a whole.&lt;/li&gt;
