&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Lead Physician to join our Virtual Health Assessment team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar Medical Group runs a Virtual Health Assessment (VHA) program that outreaches and virtually engages Oscar Health Insurance members in an evaluation and management visit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Lead Physician is responsible for delivering quality care to a panel of patients as part of a multidisciplinary team of Physicians, Advanced Practice Providers (APPs), Registered Nurses (RNs), and Medical Assistant in a virtual environment. This role will oversee a team of APPs (NPs and PAs) delivering care to their patients and supporting them in Oscar strategic initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Director of Virtual Health Assessment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Hours:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a full-time Monday–Friday schedule with 8-hour shifts. One late shift per week and one weekend per quarter are required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote position, open to candidates who reside in: Arizona; Arkansas; California; Colorado; District of Columbia; Florida; Georgia; Illinois; Massachusetts; Michigan; Nevada; New Hampshire; New Jersey; New York; North Carolina; Ohio; Pennsylvania; Texas, or Virginia.&amp;nbsp; While your daily work will be completed from your home office, occasional travel may be required for team meetings and company events. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $237,718 - $312,005 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits including generous PTO, sick and floating holidays, 9 paid holidays, 401k with match and an annual bonus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct high quality, safe patient care via telemedicine (video, phone, messaging) while working with a multidisciplinary team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide supervision to a group of APPs (NPs and PAs) who are delivering care in a virtual environment and provide professional &amp;amp; clinical growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clinical escalation point for the care delivery team as needed (APPs, RNs, MAs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of clinical guidelines, continuous improvement of care model, and participate in collaborative projects with Operations and Product team members as a clinical leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quality assurance audits in addition to required state supervisory audit requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a culture of patient safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the quality of care of your patients and ensure superior member experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct service recovery needs for Oscar patients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide growth and development of your team including management of poor performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have full practice licensure in good standing in Florida plus at least three of the following states: Arizona; Arkansas; California; Colorado; District of Columbia; Georgia; Illinois; Massachusetts; Michigan; Nevada; New Hampshire; New Jersey; New York; North Carolina; Ohio; Pennsylvania; Texas, or Virginia.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of medical residency program; specialty in Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, or Medicine-Pediatrics required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MD or DO from an ACGME accredited medical school&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ABMS Board Certification corresponding to completed residency program or additional training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of primary care [or Urgent care] experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unrestricted license to practice medicine in GA, TX, FL or IMLCC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in NP and PA supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish language fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior telehealth experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years experience in supervising teams, including other clinical staff NP and PA supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience being metric driven in a practice setting as it relates to population health management and/or, quality benchmarks, and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
