&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Senior Director, Enterprise Compliance to join our Compliance team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Enterprise Compliance supports the execution and continuous improvement of Oscar&#39;s enterprise compliance program. Reporting to the Chief Compliance Officer, you will provide leadership over key compliance functions, including regulatory compliance, regulatory change management/implementation, compliance operations, investigations, monitoring and auditing, policy governance, and compliance education. You will anticipate regulatory and industry developments, translates them into enterprise compliance priorities, and partners with cross-functional leaders to identify and mitigate compliance risks, strengthen internal controls, and promote a culture of ethics and integrity. You will exercise significant independent judgment, develops a compliance organization, and serves as a trusted advisor to business leaders on complex healthcare regulatory matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Vice President, Chief Compliance Officer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This is a remote position, open to candidates who reside in: Atlanta, GA. You will be fully remote; however, our approach to work may adapt over time. Future models could potentially involve a hybrid presence at the hub office associated with your metro area. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $196,733 - $258,212 per year.. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the execution and continuous improvement of Oscar&#39;s enterprise compliance program, including the multi-year compliance strategy, annual compliance work plans, risk assessments, policy governance, regulatory change management/implementation, monitoring, auditing, and reporting activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate enterprise compliance priorities into an relevant operating plan; establish ownership and governance; allocate resources; develop compliance managers and team members; remove barriers; and lead accountability for measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate regulatory and industry developments and advise senior leaders on their possible effects for Oscar&#39;s products, market participation, business strategy, and operating model. Provide guidance on federal and state healthcare regulations, contractual obligations, and emerging regulatory risks across applicable lines of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee compliance investigations, hotline reporting, the Special Investigations Unit, fraud-prevention activities, corrective action plans, and remediation efforts, ensuring timely resolution and appropriate escalation of significant compliance concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leaders across Legal, Privacy, Security, Internal Audit, Enterprise Risk, Clinical, Product, Operations, and People teams to embed compliance requirements into business processes and strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and uphold enterprise standards for ethics and compliance by leading education, communications, and awareness initiatives that strengthen Oscar&#39;s culture of ethics and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead compliance reporting and engagement for executive leadership, Compliance Committee, Board committees, and regulatory examinations; support interactions with regulators and external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of progressively responsible experience in healthcare compliance, regulatory affairs, legal compliance, audit, or enterprise risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; leading high-performing compliance teams and enterprise-wide compliance initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, implementing, and maintaining an effective healthcare compliance program aligned with OIG Compliance Program Guidance and applicable federal and state regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting highly regulated healthcare organizations, including health plans, managed care organizations, healthcare technology companies, provider organizations, or related entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of anticipating regulatory developments and translating them into enterprise priorities, operating plans, and business controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex compliance investigations, monitoring and auditing activities, regulatory risk assessments, corrective action planning, and policy governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising senior business leaders on complex regulatory and operational compliance issues and leading their resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, experience presenting to executive leadership, governance committees, regulators, or external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Marketplace and other applicable government or commercial health-plan products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading compliance in a technology-enabled, rapidly scaling, or operationally complex healthcare organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data, technology, and automation to improve compliance monitoring, reporting, and program effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare compliance certification such as CHC, CHPC, CCEP, or comparable certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD, master&#39;s degree, or other relevant advanced education.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
