&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Senior Director, Strategic Finance and Enterprise Planning to join our Strategic Finance team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director of Strategic Finance &amp;amp; Enterprise role will help lead the annual operating plan cycle, partnering with Finance, Strategy, and business leaders to translate company priorities into financial plans, targets, and executive-ready materials. You will also drive the strategic investment process by building business cases, evaluating trade-offs, and supporting resource allocation toward the company&#39;s highest-priority initiatives. You bring FP&amp;amp;A or strategic finance experience, excellent financial modeling and the judgment to influence senior stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the VP, FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our New York City office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $218,592 - $286,902 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead key components of the annual operating plan cycle, partnering with Finance, Strategy, and business leaders to translate company priorities into financial plans, targets, and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business leaders to evaluate strategic investment opportunities, assess trade-offs, and ensure capital and operating resources are allocated against the company&#39;s highest-priority initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial models, business cases, and decision frameworks to support investment prioritization, ROI assessment, and long-range value creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear reporting and insights on plan performance, investment progress, risks, and opportunities for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executive discussions by synthesizing complex financial and operational inputs into concise recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve planning accuracy, resource allocation, and investment discipline across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in finance, FP&amp;amp;A, corporate strategy, investment banking, consulting, or a related strategic finance role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or supporting annual planning, budgeting, forecasting, long-range planning, or capital allocation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling, analytical, and business case development skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence senior stakeholders and drive alignment across cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to turn analysis into clear executive-level recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills and comfort operating in complex, fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of ownership, and ability to balance strategic thinking with operational execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in similar roles in strategy consulting, financial services, or insurance industries (ex: private equity, venture capital, investment banking)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong preference for healthcare industry experience and deep market knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degrees or professional designations, such as an MBA or CFA.&lt;/li&gt;
